ENVIRONMENT
node_modules
venv
.env
# Editor and agent rule files. These are copies of AGENTS.md that individual
# tools drop into the folder; they belong to the machine, not the launcher.
# Named explicitly rather than with a bare `.*`, because that would also
# ignore this file, and a clone would arrive with no ignore rules at all.
.clinerules
.cursorrules
.geminiignore
.windsurfrules
# Skills the agent tooling downloads on demand, plus the lock file recording
# what it fetched. Both are reproducible from the user-level copy.
#
# Every tool gets its own mirror of the same skills under its own dot folder,
# so they are listed rather than folded into a `.*` rule, which would also take
# .gitignore itself and the other named files with it. `skills/` is the same
# mirror one level up.
.agents/
skills/
skills-lock.json
.autohand/
.claude/
.codeartsdoer/
.codebuddy/
.codemaker/
.codestudio/
.commandcode/
.continue/
# Cursor's own editor settings, for the same reason as the folders above: it is
# written by the editor on the machine, and `.cursorrules` is already ignored
# above.
.cursor/
.grok/
.jazz/
.openhands/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~*
/logs/
/cache/
# Coverage output, if a run ever writes it. The suite uses node --test with no
# reporter configured, so this exists for a local `c8` run rather than for CI.
coverage/
/.npm/
*.tsbuildinfo
# The SQLite database, its WAL/SHM siblings, the generated session secret, the
# live-process lock, and the backups directory. All of it is rebuilt by
# `npm run migrate` plus the reference import, and none of it belongs in version
# control - except the backups, which are the only copy of anything not
# re-imported, and are ignored by the same rule only because they sit inside it.
# If KIP_DATA_DIR is pointed somewhere else, that directory needs its own rule.
app/data/
# The demonstration database, at the launcher root rather than under `app`. It is
# a generated artefact like the real one - rebuilt by `npm run seed:demo` or by the
# `demo.js` launcher step - and it is invented content, so it is the last thing that
# belongs in version control. It also sits outside `app/`, so the `app/data/` rule
# above does not reach it.
data-demo/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/GEMINI.md
/QWEN.md
/SPEC.md
